  "unit": "u03-family",
  "title": "Review: my family",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Last new words: **স্বামী** (*shami*, husband) and **স্ত্রী** (*stri*, wife). In everyday speech many people say **বউ** (*bou*) for 'wife' — it also means 'bride'. (The ব in স্বামী is silent, which you'll learn about in the conjuncts script unit.)\n\nQuick recap of the family map:\n\n- **Father's side:** দাদা / দাদি (grandparents) · চাচা / চাচি (his brother and his wife) · ফুফু / ফুফা (his sister and her husband)\n- **Mother's side:** নানা / নানি (grandparents) · মামা / মামি (her brother and his wife) · খালা / খালু (her sister and her husband)\n- **ছেলে / মেয়ে** = son / daughter as well as boy / girl\n\nOne more reminder: in Bangladesh **দাদা** is your *grandfather*. If a friend from Kolkata says *dada*, they probably mean an elder brother.\n\nTo join two ideas with 'but', use **কিন্তু**: **আমার ভাই আছে, কিন্তু বোন নেই।** When you hear a word you don't know, ask **X মানে কী?** \"What does X mean?\". **সবাই কেমন আছে?** \"How is everyone?\" is the classic question about someone's family.",
